{"kind":"assert","text":"AR-3 report (read-only: Workers logs and DO analytics, dap-grow version fc8be51e, main 305342f8, which includes AS-2). Evidence: artroom-evidence/2026-11-17-ar3-grow-archive.\n\n1. WHICH SCOPES. All four archivable scopes of grow-demo fail their archive at the AR-1 cap, once an hour at :35:\n- Directory sc_cu5bjlh3… (object 661c0b32);\n- Rules sc_kqwvpcc2… (9ecbec54);\n- Site sc_axnkexzg… (236dc9fd);\n- Room A sc_zp7zb2bj… (e90a0152).\nEvery archive-pass-diagnostic-v1 line from 10:55Z to 13:10Z outside step 'pin' is one of eight passes, all identical at 11:35:09-23 and 12:35:09-24: step target, state retry, reason unavailable, detail target-missing, attemptsAtLoad 0. Each archive-row-diagnostic-v1 shows no row (state absent), storedWake.pending true and next at :35 of the next hour. The Directory alarm fires first. Its pass reads the other three through archiveItem and nativeBirth, and each of those runs its own pass. The cost rises along the chain: inputWork 1.4 M, 1.5 M, 20.9 M and 40.2 M; calls 18, 19, 27 and 35.\nAS-2's stopCause is absent because no budget stop happens: the pass returns through done() at packages/scope/src/archive-driver.ts:276, and detail target-missing names the cause. Membership sc_kp744f2i… (e3b2c953) makes a cheap 'pin disabled' pass every minute (admit excludes membership, apps/room/archive.ts:48). That pass follows the simulator's minute cadence and has nothing to do with the hourly pattern.\n\n2. WHY. target.resolve finds no archive repository for this room. It returns null when the Directory's repository row lacks archive \"journal\", a repository or a destination ref, or when the destination or branch does not match (packages/scope/src/archive-target.ts:138-145; apps/room/archive.ts returns null without a repository). The driver then reports target-missing and re-defers the wake (archive-driver.ts:266-277). The backoff grows to the 3600 s cap (archive-driver.ts:90-95) and has no end. The grow-demo room was made on 14 Nov, before AE-1, and never bound an archive destination, so no pass can ever find a target. One read would confirm this: the Directory's 'repository' items, read through the operator's growmcp items. I did not make that read: it needs the operator home.\n\n3. COST per hour, from per-object DO invocations 12:30Z-12:46Z against the flat 49 per minute: 12:35 +72 (121), 12:36 +12 (61), 12:40 +8 (57), 12:41 +6 (55). About 98 extra DO requests per hour, about 2,350 per day. They fall on the four scopes above and on object 71671c0f, which writes no archive diagnostics and takes +33 at :35. The :40-:41 pair holds no archive pass. It falls on 71671c0f, Room A and Membership five minutes after the burst, which matches the outbox retry cap of 300 s (packages/contract/src/bounds.ts:129) after the :35 calls. That attribution is inferred; no log line names it. The CPU per burst is large for nothing gained: about 64 M inputWork units of budgeted work.\n\n4. RECOMMENDATION: a small code fix, AR-4, rather than an operator bind. A room with no archive destination is a definite answer, not a transient failure. When the Directory's repository row is absent, or lacks archive \"journal\", the pass should end 'disabled' with next null, the way 'pin disabled' does. A later bind-repository act would then signal the wake again. Real unavailability, such as an unreadable reply or a timeout, keeps retrying. Every room made without a destination pays this cost today, and Lending shows 0 only because its rooms have one or have stopped. If Hugh wants Grow archived instead, the operator binds a destination for grow-demo and the retries end in a confirmed pass. In both cases, the benign interim cost is about 98 requests per hour.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}